===Etymology 2===
From {{etyl|enm|en}} {{m|enm|soke}}, {{m|enm|sok}}, {{m|enm|soc}}, from {{etyl|ang|en}} {{m|ang|sōcn}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|en}} {{m|gem-pro|*sōkniz}}.

====Alternative forms====
* {{l|en|sock}}, {{l|en|soke}}

====Noun====
{{en-noun|?}}

# {{label|en|UK|legal|obsolete}} The [[lord]]'s power or [[privilege]] of holding a [[court]] in a [[district]], as in [[manor]] or [[lordship]]; [[jurisdiction]] of [[cause]]s, and the limits of that jurisdiction.
# {{label|en|UK|obsolete}} [[liberty|Liberty]] or privilege of [[tenant]]s excused from customary burdens.
# {{label|en|UK|obsolete}} An exclusive privilege formerly claimed by [[miller]]s of [[grind]]ing all the [[corn]] used within the manor or township in which the [[mill]] stands.

